OCMAT 1
# Written by the Aver Engine editor.
# NeonDistrict: "Night market stall" by Allen Tseng (@alen60303), CC BY 4.0 -- https://sketchfab.com/3d-models/night-market-stall-ffaabf87bb024b48b240909632e0b524
NAME NeonDistrict_sf60_Material
SHADER standard
BLEND opaque
CULL none
FLAGS twosided=1 castshadow=1 worlduv=0

PARAM baseColorFactor 1 1 1 1
PARAM metallicFactor 0
PARAM roughnessFactor 1
# Emissive in engine units: 1 = a white wall in full sun, about 33,000 cd/m2. Peak 0.12 = about 4,000 cd/m2:
# painted-in blue screen glow on the main structure: the large roof TV sign (z 5.1-6.1 m) and three small roof monitors (z about 5.0-5.5 m), plus blue window panes and thin blue neon strips on the tower. There is no emissive map, the glow is baked in the albedo (saturated blue about RGB 40/120/255 with light-cyan glyphs); build an emissive mask from those saturated-blue pixels only, the rest of the material is dark rusty metal and must stay unlit..
PARAM emissiveFactor 0.12 0.12 0.12
PARAM normalScale 1
PARAM occlusionStrength 1
PARAM reflectance 0.04
PARAM f90 1
PARAM ior 1.5
PARAM transmission 0
PARAM uvTiling 200

TEX baseColor {path:Textures/NeonDistrict/material_baseColor.png} uv0 sRGB
